{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-05-recovery-successor.md at exact d90b84ac08183e2b642d869c1cf938c7298b0d89 on request/recovery-successor, under promise git:sha1…110b0e5 on request git:sha1…1f9cbca\n\nRecovery successor, revision 8 at d90b84ac08183e2b642d869c1cf938c7298b0d89, answering the checker's changes-requested verdict 304bce75 on e865fd05: the note, its corrections and the acceptance map. The authority note's revision 20 (4ef1a5e3) and the scope contract's revision 15 are now named as adopted and in force throughout; revision 7 still called them proposed. What is in force today, stated plainly: the adopted authority note keeps one conservative rule until this design and IA agree on the supervisor's side: no cut is final and no commit ends a host. So a stopped task's host ends only by a person's end-host, by the provider's own event, or by a restore that replaces the instance; every checkpoint is saved as of its cut. The fenced-root save act is in force; whether a supervisor can cut a fenced instance is asked of IA. The restore guard is in no row of the adopted definition, so it is the runtime's rule only; asks C1 to C4 stand; C5 is met and withdrawn, since the adopted answer on pins and deadlines is taken into section 10. Table 14.8: it is now labelled a history under revision 18 and not a witness of the reservations in force. The arithmetic, by script: with the adopted standing save room added, row 0 is 65 of 64 checkpoint places and 9 of 8 cut places, and 15 of the table's 24 place cells exceed their maximum. No example replaces it, because none can be built without shared places, a larger maximum or a smaller closure, and this note invents none. A finding for the capacity owner (cc570904), the proof plan and the authority note's owner, stated in section 12.9: counting each room's places side by side as the adopted rows state, an idle task holds 6 cut places, which fits, but the apply that makes it run must also hold the pause room, 9 against a maximum of 8; so a task can be established but cannot be made to run. The count is of the rows as written; row P11 and the count guards were not read, and the adopted note itself says the fit is unproved. The authority note's revision 22, in progress, is asked to decide whether the rooms share one closure. Acceptance map: 68 rows, 45 designed, 21 depends, 2 unresolved, no row changed. Reading limit, stated in the note and short of what was asked: sections 12.1.7 and 5.9 of the adopted authority note are known from a full reading at its revision 17 plus complete differences to revisions 18 and 20, not from a fresh reading as they stand; section 5.8 was read as it stands except one range. Design only: nothing was run.","body":{"commit":"d90b84ac08183e2b642d869c1cf938c7298b0d89","path":"notes/2026-10-05-recovery-successor.md"}}